---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
import { requiresConsent } from '../lib/consent';
const updated = '29 October 2026';
// Drafts stay out of search until counsel signs off and every placeholder is filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;

// The choice as the server sees it, so the switch below starts in the right place.
const ask = requiresConsent(Astro.locals.country);
const chosen = Astro.cookies.get('cm_consent')?.value;
const state = chosen === '1' ? 'on' : chosen === '0' ? 'off' : ask ? 'unset' : 'default';
---

<Base title="Cookie policy · Comarket" description="Every cookie and browser store comarket.si uses, what each is for, how long it lasts, and how to change your choice." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Cookie policy"
    lede="A short list: one cookie for your choice, three for analytics if you allow them, and Cloudflare's security checks."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/cookies"
  >
    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <div class="short" id="cookie-choice" data-state={state}>
      <p data-status>
        {state === 'on' && 'Analytics are on for this browser.'}
        {state === 'off' && 'Analytics are off for this browser.'}
        {state === 'unset' && 'You haven’t chosen yet, so analytics are off.'}
        {state === 'default' && 'Where you are, analytics are on unless you turn them off.'}
      </p>
      <div class="choice-row">
        <button type="button" class="btn ghost" data-set="0">Turn analytics off</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-set="1">Allow analytics</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      Your choice is saved in this browser only, so make it again on other devices. Turning analytics off deletes the visitor
      ID cookie and the side cookie, and stops new events; it doesn't delete events already recorded. To have those deleted,
      email [[PRIVACY EMAIL]].
    </p>

    <h2>How we decide whether to ask</h2>
    <p>
      Our host, Cloudflare, tells our server which country a request comes from. In the EU, the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, and
      whenever the country is unknown, we set no analytics cookie until you choose "Allow". Everywhere else analytics are on
      by default, and you can turn them off above. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as
      turning analytics off.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies we set</h2>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th><th>Type</th><th>Set when</th><th>Lasts</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cm_consent</code></td>
            <td>Remembers whether you allowed analytics, so we don't ask again</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary</td>
            <td>You make a choice</td>
            <td>180 days</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cm_vid</code></td>
            <td>A random ID that links your visits, the page versions you saw and simple events, so we can tell which pages work. It contains no name, email or IP address, and scripts on the page can't read it</td>
            <td>Analytics</td>
            <td>Analytics are allowed</td>
            <td>1 year</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cm_x_pricing_v1</code></td>
            <td>Keeps the version of the brands page you were assigned in a pricing test, so you see the same one each visit and the rates you saw are recorded if you join</td>
            <td>Analytics (testing)</td>
            <td>You open the brands page with analytics allowed</td>
            <td>180 days</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cm_side</code></td>
            <td>Remembers whether you last chose the brands or the creators page, so the home page takes you back there</td>
            <td>Preference</td>
            <td>You open the brands or creators page with analytics allowed</td>
            <td>180 days</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>All four are first-party cookies, sent only to comarket.si over encrypted connections.</p>

    <h2>Cloudflare security</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare protects the site from attacks and bots. To do that it may set its own strictly necessary cookies, such as
      <code>__cf_bm</code> (about 30 minutes), <code>cf_clearance</code> (after a security check, for the period the site's
      security settings allow) and <code>_cfuvid</code> (until you close the browser). When bot checks are switched on, the
      waitlist form loads Cloudflare Turnstile from challenges.cloudflare.com, which looks at signals from your browser and
      device to tell people from bots. Cloudflare says it doesn't use this information to track you across sites or for
      advertising; see Cloudflare's Turnstile privacy addendum and cookie policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Other browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you open the home page with a <code>?trip=</code> link (we use these to test page transitions), the page remembers
      which transition you picked in session storage under <code>cm-trip</code>. It is cleared when you close the tab. Saving
      your pass image creates the file in your browser; nothing is stored.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't use</h2>
    <p>
      No advertising or retargeting cookies, no third-party analytics, no social media pixels, and no fonts or scripts from
      ad networks. Our fonts are served from our own site.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we add a cookie, we will list it here first, with a new date. If it needs consent, we will ask for it before setting
      it. Questions: <a href="mailto:[[PRIVACY EMAIL]]">[[PRIVACY EMAIL]]</a>. More about how we use the data is in our
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .choice-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .choice-row .btn {
    --h: 44px;
    padding: 0 18px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const TEXT: Record<string, string> = {
    '1': 'Analytics are on for this browser.',
    '0': 'Analytics are off for this browser.',
  };
  function bind() {
    const box = document.getElementById('cookie-choice');
    if (!box || box.dataset.bound) return;
    box.dataset.bound = '1';
    const status = box.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!;
    box.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-set]').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const value = b.dataset.set!;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/api/consent', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ value }),
          });
          if (!res.ok) throw new Error(String(res.status));
          status.textContent = TEXT[value];
          box.dataset.state = value === '1' ? 'on' : 'off';
          // the banner, if it's open, has nothing left to ask
          const banner = document.getElementById('consent');
          if (banner) banner.hidden = true;
        } catch {
          status.textContent = 'That didn’t save. Check your connection and try again.';
        }
      }),
    );
  }
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', bind);
</script>
